448 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 449 0 R/Alt(A chart with one row per measured case, each labeled with the structure and its source, and a horizontal axis from -31 to +35 percent change of the resonance frequency from low level to the highest level tested. Rows are grouped under six colored headings. Well-tightened bolted joints: nine rows, all between about -0.1 and -4 percent, inside a gray band from -0.1 to -4 percent. Lightly torqued or friction joints: a two-beam structure at about -6 percent, a slug in press-fit foam cups at about -8 to -10 percent under shaker sine, one bolt at about -10 percent under shaker random. Bolted joint in macroslip: a Brake-Reuss beam at about -28 percent. Measured at shock level: the foam-cup slug at 0 percent under shaker shock pulses, and a resonant plate from -1.6 to -12.7 percent on five modes and +19.8 percent on one, between a hammer test and projectile shocks. Bolted joint hardening, cause not identified: the S4 beam's first mode at about +1.6 percent. Geometry: rows from -12 percent (a curved beam clamped by bolted joints) to +32 percent (a cantilever with a clamped thin strip), with thin plates at about +13 and +18 percent, a curved panel at about -7 to -8 percent, a bolted curved panel at about -3 to -7 percent before rising again, and a cross beam at +4.7 percent. Marker shape gives the excitation: circle for hammer, square for shaker, triangle for shaker shock pulses, diamond for a hammer test compared with projectile shock, plus sign for a hammer test compared with a shaker. Filled markers are numbers stated in the source's text; open markers were read off a figure's axis.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 1184 0 R>>
endobj
